1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,578
SHIRLEY:

2
00:00:02,578 --> 00:00:02,700
Hello?

3
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:03,848
TOM:

4
00:00:03,848 --> 00:00:04,331
Oh hello.

5
00:00:04,331 --> 00:00:08,680
I was hoping to speak to Jack Fitzgerald about renting a cottage.

6
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:08,730
SHIRLEY:

7
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:10,202
I'm his wife, Shirley,

8
00:00:10,202 --> 00:00:12,029
and we own the cottages together,

9
00:00:12,029 --> 00:00:14,160
so I'm sure I can help you.

10
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,210
TOM:

11
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:15,148
Great.

12
00:00:15,148 --> 00:00:16,630
My name's Tom.

13
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:20,266
Some friends of ours rented Granary Cottage from you last year,

14
00:00:20,266 --> 00:00:22,250
and they thought it was great.

15
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:26,040
So my wife and I are hoping to come in May for a week.

16
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:26,360
SHIRLEY:

17
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,600
What date did you have in mind?

18
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,056
TOM:

19
00:00:29,056 --> 00:00:32,250
The week beginning the 14th, if possible.

20
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:32,772
SHIRLEY:

21
00:00:32,772 --> 00:00:34,337
I'll just check ...

22
00:00:34,337 --> 00:00:38,510
I'm sorry, Tom, it's already booked that week.

23
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:43,480
It's free the week beginning the 28th, though, for seven nights.

24
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,118
In fact,

25
00:00:44,118 --> 00:00:47,310
that's the only time you could have it in May.

26
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:47,737
TOM:

27
00:00:47,737 --> 00:00:48,163
Oh.

28
00:00:48,163 --> 00:00:51,150
Well, we could manage that, I think.

29
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:54,460
We'd just need to change a couple of things.

30
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,540
How much would it cost?

31
00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:57,004
SHIRLEY:

32
00:00:57,004 --> 00:00:59,790
That's the beginning of high season,

33
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:03,040
so it'd be ￡550 for the week.

34
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:03,398
TOM:

35
00:01:03,398 --> 00:01:03,755
Ah.

36
00:01:03,755 --> 00:01:07,690
That's a bit more than we wanted to pay, I'm afraid.

37
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:12,130
We've budgeted up to ￡500 for accommodation.

38
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:12,617
SHIRLEY:

39
00:01:12,617 --> 00:01:17,486
Well, we've just finished converting another building into a cottage,

40
00:01:17,486 --> 00:01:19,920
which we're calling Chervil Cottage.

41
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:20,287
TOM:

42
00:01:20,287 --> 00:01:20,653
Sorry?

43
00:01:20,653 --> 00:01:22,120
What was that again?

44
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,517
SHIRLEY:

45
00:01:23,517 --> 00:01:24,913
Chervil.

46
00:01:24,913 --> 00:01:30,500
C-H-E-R-V for Victor I-L.

47
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:30,831
TOM:

48
00:01:30,831 --> 00:01:31,163
Oh,

49
00:01:31,163 --> 00:01:32,820
that's a herb, isn't it?

50
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:33,241
SHIRLEY:

51
00:01:33,241 --> 00:01:34,083
That's right.

52
00:01:34,083 --> 00:01:36,610
It grows fairly wild around here.

53
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:41,160
You could have that for the week you want for ￡480.

54
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:41,551
TOM:

55
00:01:41,551 --> 00:01:41,942
OK.

56
00:01:41,942 --> 00:01:45,460
So could you tell me something about it, please?

57
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:45,914
SHIRLEY:

58
00:01:45,914 --> 00:01:46,822
Of course.

59
00:01:46,822 --> 00:01:50,000
The building was built as a garage.

60
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,080
It's a little smaller than Granary Cottage.

61
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:53,378
TOM:

62
00:01:53,378 --> 00:01:55,760
So that must sleep two people, as well?

63
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,159
SHIRLEY:

64
00:01:56,159 --> 00:01:56,956
That's right.

65
00:01:56,956 --> 00:01:58,550
There's a double bedroom.

66
00:01:58,550 --> 00:01:58,758
TOM:

67
00:01:58,758 --> 00:01:59,800
Does it have a garden?

68
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,194
SHIRLEY:

69
00:02:00,194 --> 00:02:04,928
Yes, you get to it from the living room through French doors,

70
00:02:04,928 --> 00:02:06,900
and we provide two deckchairs.

71
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:10,052
We hope to build a patio in the near future,

72
00:02:10,052 --> 00:02:13,520
but I wouldn't like to guarantee it'll be finished by May.

73
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:13,925
TOM:

74
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:14,330
OK.

75
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:14,993
SHIRLEY:

76
00:02:14,993 --> 00:02:20,297
The front door opens onto the old farmyard,

77
00:02:20,297 --> 00:02:29,580
and parking isn't a problem – there's plenty of room at the front for that.

78
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:30,049
TOM:

79
00:02:30,049 --> 00:02:32,860
What about facilities in the cottage?

80
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:37,160
It has standard things like a cooker and fridge, I presume.

81
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:37,589
SHIRLEY:

82
00:02:37,589 --> 00:02:43,591
In the kitchen area there's a fridge-freezer and we've just put in an electric

83
00:02:43,591 --> 00:02:44,020
cooker.

84
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:46,290
Is there a washing machine?

85
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:46,714
TOM:

86
00:02:46,714 --> 00:02:47,139
Yes.

87
00:02:47,139 --> 00:02:50,533
There's also a TV in the living room,

88
00:02:50,533 --> 00:02:52,230
which plays DVDs too.

89
00:02:52,230 --> 00:02:55,941
The bathroom is too small for a bath,

90
00:02:55,941 --> 00:02:58,260
so there's a shower instead.

91
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:01,780
I think a lot of people prefer that nowadays, anyway.

92
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:02,169
TOM:

93
00:03:02,169 --> 00:03:04,500
It's more environmentally friendly, isn't it?

94
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,600
Unless you spend half the day in it!

95
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:06,925
SHIRLEY:

96
00:03:06,925 --> 00:03:07,250
Exactly.

97
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:07,601
TOM:

98
00:03:07,601 --> 00:03:08,656
What about heating?

99
00:03:08,656 --> 00:03:12,170
It sometimes gets quite cool at that time of year.

100
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:12,507
SHIRLEY:

101
00:03:12,507 --> 00:03:13,519
There's central heating,

102
00:03:13,519 --> 00:03:17,230
and if you want to light a fire, there's a stove.

103
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:20,520
We can provide all the wood you need for it.

104
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,927
It smells so much nicer than coal,

105
00:03:22,927 --> 00:03:27,740
and it makes the room very cosy – we've got one in our own house.

106
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:28,088
TOM:

107
00:03:28,088 --> 00:03:29,480
That sounds very pleasant.

108
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:33,060
Perhaps we should come in the winter, to make the most of it!

109
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:33,333
SHIRLEY:

110
00:03:33,333 --> 00:03:37,157
Yes, we find we don't want to go out when we've got the fire

111
00:03:37,157 --> 00:03:37,430
burning.

112
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:40,650
There are some attractive views from the cottage,

113
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:42,260
which I haven't mentioned.

114
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:46,739
There's a famous stone bridge – it's one of the oldest in the region,

115
00:03:46,739 --> 00:03:49,840
and you can see it from the living room.

116
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:51,700
It isn't far away.

117
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:54,536
The bedroom window looks in the opposite direction,

118
00:03:54,536 --> 00:03:59,500
and has a lovely view of the hills and the monument at the top.

119
00:03:59,500 --> 00:03:59,977
TOM:

120
00:03:59,977 --> 00:04:00,453
Well,

121
00:04:00,453 --> 00:04:02,360
that all sounds perfect.

122
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,198
I'd like to book it, please.

123
00:04:04,198 --> 00:04:05,730
Would you want a deposit?

124
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:06,276
SHIRLEY:

125
00:04:06,276 --> 00:04:11,732
Yes, we ask for thirty percent to secure your booking,

126
00:04:11,732 --> 00:04:14,460
so that'll be, um, ￡144.

127
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:14,715
TOM:

128
00:04:14,715 --> 00:04:17,270
And when would you like the rest of the money?

129
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:17,673
SHIRLEY:

130
00:04:17,673 --> 00:04:19,287
You're coming in May,

131
00:04:19,287 --> 00:04:22,110
so the last day of March, please.

132
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:22,635
TOM:

133
00:04:22,635 --> 00:04:23,160
Fine.

134
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,765
SHIRLEY:

135
00:04:23,765 --> 00:04:24,370
Excellent.

136
00:04:24,370 --> 00:04:28,000
Could I just take your details ...
